tip: | Look at the two props. | A bench and a mailbox, each just a handful of parts. Small things read through a clear silhouette, not through detail.
tip: 2 | Parts first. | Planks, legs, box and post get one color each. If two parts merge here, the outline will not separate them later.
tip: 4 | One red flag. | One small accent does a lot: the flag says mailbox more than the box does. Keep accents few, and in a color the piece does not otherwise use.
tip: 5 | Sel-out keeps it soft. | Each outline pixel is one step darker than the art beside it, so the wood gets a brown line and the box a blue one. A black line would look stuck on.
tip: | Try it. | Pick the bench planks with the Color picker and step one with Lighten / Darken to see a plank stand out. | shade
